{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1792 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ed578e93db308f2e59c5ea8c09bd786e3d8a74816c19fb80289f8b81c0a9fc21" :edb/db-before-t 1791 :edb/db-after-t 1792 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535104 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:56:20.581Z" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184009 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184009 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}$.*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}w + w|= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom __] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535104 false] [17592186184009 1145 "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}w + w &= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]]\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535104 false] [17592186184009 1145 "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184038 1100 "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,.$*\n\n- the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n\n- $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n\n- addition of polynomials is not commutative" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184038 1100 "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,$.*\n\n1. the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n2. $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n3. addition of polynomials is not commutative" 13194139535104 false] [17592186184038 1145 "The correct answer  is as follows:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.** *\n\nFor instance, if $p(x) = 1 +x^3$ and $q(x) = 1-x^3$, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V.$ However  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & =(1+{x}^{3})+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2\\notin V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3.$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184038 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.***\n\nFor instance, if\n\n$$\np(x) = 1 +x^3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nq(x) = 1-x^3\n$$\n\n, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V$. However\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(x) + q(x) &= (1 + x^{3}) + (1 - x^{3}) \\\\\n&= 2 ∉ V\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3$." 13194139535104 false] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331353 13194139535104 true] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331360 13194139535104 true] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331373 13194139535104 true] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331380 13194139535104 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331332 13194139535104 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331339 13194139535104 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331346 13194139535104 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331387 13194139535104 true] [17592186184703 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535104 true] [17592186184703 1100 "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x ∈ R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $_________$.*" 13194139535104 false] [17592186184703 1100 "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184703 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184704 1017 #edb/ref 17592186183113 13194139535104 false] [17592186184704 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331367 13194139535104 true] [17592186184704 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535104 true] [17592186184704 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[A1] - [A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *$α0 = 0$ for any $α ∈ R$*\n\n*Proof:*\n$\\begin{bmatrix}α0|= α0 & [given] \\\\ α0|= α(0 + 0) & [axiom A3] \\\\ α0|= α0 + α0 & [axiom __] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= (α0 + α0) + (- α0) & [add- α0to both sides] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= α0 + (α0 + (- α0)) & [axiom A2] \\\\ 0|= α0 + 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ 0|= α0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535104 false] [17592186184704 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$\\alpha 0=0$ for any $\\alpha \\in R$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186184704 1145 "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A8}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331333 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1089 "q-106813" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1100 "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1113 #uuid "1cd61265-dcc6-5f89-bc03-f1168b91584b" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331332 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331334 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331335 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331336 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331337 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331338 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1041 "selection" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331334 13194139535104 true] [17592186331333 1110 #uuid "1768b600-a256-5baa-8032-a21788f16c7e" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331334 1034 "$F$ does not contain the zero element" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331334 1111 #uuid "042dc0fb-357e-59c1-8d04-096ccfbb7570" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331335 1034 "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331335 1111 #uuid "1ce21c01-f17a-54b1-beb0-cac4f6946d6f" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331336 1034 "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331336 1111 #uuid "75f11239-8a13-52a6-b25f-87a13580da05" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331337 1034 "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331337 1111 #uuid "824101ce-ad6e-5d33-8b0a-2323495b2b6b" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331338 1034 "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331338 1111 #uuid "e1f13a8f-3c54-58b4-97f3-8683bc95d71e" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331340 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1089 "q-106929" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1100 "Let $Y$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree exactly $2.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1113 #uuid "4c206776-99db-55ba-ae48-7c0ec7d6d597" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331339 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{2}+x$ and $q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$ Then $p,q\\in Y,$ but \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)={x}^{2}+x+(-{x}^{2})=x\\notin Y\n$$\n\n because $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)=1\\ne 2.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- $1\\cdot p=p$ for all $p\\in Y.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331341 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331342 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331343 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331344 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331345 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1041 "selection" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331343 13194139535104 true] [17592186331340 1110 #uuid "91cae22a-4346-52fb-a7f4-10f70ab881db" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331341 1034 "addition of polynomials is not associative" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331341 1111 #uuid "4688d73b-9179-5ae6-ae97-603ba62dfce0" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331342 1034 "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331342 1111 #uuid "b8eabd34-2b3b-55a1-96ab-ab60b97e5c23" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331343 1034 "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331343 1111 #uuid "e38ba574-7ad3-5ad2-81ce-e27fc819db61" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331344 1034 "addition of polynomials is not commutative" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331344 1111 #uuid "e13ec148-f3af-5f03-8b5f-2dbeeceac2c4" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331345 1034 "$1\\cdot p\\ne p$ for some $p\\in Y$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535104 true] [17592186331345 1111 #uuid "62aaa84f-a336-5fb0-96dc-f7020990aa8c" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331347 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1089 "q-106933" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1100 "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1113 #uuid "17d56701-363e-5629-ba43-f0ff54124002" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331346 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331348 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331349 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331350 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331351 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331352 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1041 "selection" 13194139535104 true] [17592186331347 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331352 13194139535104 true] [